[24.64309, "o", "   - File paths other than the required input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' and output redirections should not appear in the args\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.643104, "o", "> "]
[24.643183, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.643202, "o", "> "]
[24.643413, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[24.643441, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.643463, "o", "**Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.643549, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.64358, "o", "> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[24.643605, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.643646, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.643674, "o", "> "]
[24.643753, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.643795, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.643883, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.643975, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644041, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644073, "o", "  },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644094, "o", "]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[24.644109, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644126, "o", "**Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644145, "o", "> "]
[24.644234, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644259, "o", "> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[24.644275, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644331, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[24.644356, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644409, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644425, "o", "> "]
[24.644469, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644487, "o", "> "]
[24.644547, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644562, "o", "> "]
[24.644618, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644632, "o", "> "]
[24.644724, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644749, "o", "  },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644764, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644781, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[24.644799, "o", "**Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[24.644813, "o", "> "]
[24.644946, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
